    <string name="reveal_every_safe_square_to_win_a_number_tells">Reveal every safe square to win. A number tells you how many mines touch that square, including diagonally.</string>
    <string name="tap_to_reveal_hold_a_covered_square_to_flag">Tap to reveal. Hold a covered square to flag it, or turn on Flag mode to place flags with taps. Tap a flag in Flag mode, or hold it, to remove it.</string>
    <string name="tap_a_revealed_number_when_you_have_placed_the">Tap a revealed number when you have placed the matching number of flags around it to open its other neighbors. Incorrect flags can uncover a mine!</string>
    <string name="a_hold_flags_once_and_never_reveals_moving_into">A hold flags once and never reveals. Moving into another cell cancels the move. When squares are too small to tap reliably, your first touch zooms in; lift and touch again to play.</string>
    <string name="pinch_to_zoom_and_drag_to_explore_fit_board">Pinch to zoom and drag to explore. Fit board shows the entire field. Your first reveal always opens a safe area; later moves may require a guess.</string>
    <string name="no_guess_preset_boards_are_verified_solvable_by_deduction">No-guess preset boards are verified solvable by deduction. Practice offers hints and undo, without changing normal records. Daily challenges use a fixed opening and count only the first attempt.</string>
    <string name="your_game_saves_automatically_the_clock_pauses_while_menus">Your game saves automatically. The clock pauses while menus are open or the app is in the background.</string>
    <string name="optional_question_marks_are_available_in_settings_they_mark">Optional question marks are available in Settings. They mark uncertainty and never count toward a chord. Finished regular boards can be retried in practice with the same mine layout.</string>
